Initvdu.doc-----------This is an utility to initialise the user's login terminal.If called with no parameters it sends the 'is' initialisation string in /dd/sys/termcap to stdout. It is intended for use in .login.If the -r option is present the 'rs' (reset) string is sent instead.The -a=xx option can be used to send any non-parameterised capability stringdefined in /dd/sys/termcap. For instance, -a=cl sends the 'clear screen' string. See the accompanying 'cls' script for a practical example.Author	Martin Gregorie	10 Sadlers Mead	Harlow	Essex	CM18 6HG	Gregorie@LFGMS.logica.com